   "subject": "confidence interval code from StackOverflow seems to be broken with newer ggplot2 and Hmisc",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi,</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m new to ggplot2 and this group so first off, if this sort of post is inappropriate here, please do let me know.  I very much like the idea of using a summary statistic to plot a confidence interval directly from a dataset without needing to use dplyr to generate that confidence interval.  I found a great example of how to do this on <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/32669473/plotting-the-means-with-confidence-intervals-with-ggplot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/32669473/plotting-the-means-with-confidence-intervals-with-ggplot&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368230643000&amp;usg=AOvVaw27w_DCELUG3Gq4LZ7Ai1qA\">StackOverflow</a>, and I paste the code at the end of this question.  My problem is that this code works great with: ggplot2_0.9.3.1 and Hmisc_3.14-0, but when I run it with ggplot2_2.2.0 and Hmisc_3.17-1, I get this error:    <font color=\"#ff0000\">Error: Unknown parameters: width, <a href=\"http://conf.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://conf.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368230643000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0n_nlcWgE5gWSaLLKp4JXT\">conf.int</a></font></div><div><br></div><div>I have a two part questions.  </div><div>1) Why am I getting this error and how do I fix it?  </div><div>2) As a newbie, how am I supposed to figure out the cause of this error on my own?</div><div><br></div><div>For #2, I tried looking in the documentation for geom_ribbon and stat_summary in both the old and new ggplot2 and I just don&#39;t see any mention of <a href=\"http://conf.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://conf.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368230643000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0n_nlcWgE5gWSaLLKp4JXT\">conf.int</a>.  So how am I supposed to figure out how the old ribbon geometry used <a href=\"http://conf.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://conf.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368230643000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0n_nlcWgE5gWSaLLKp4JXT\">conf.int</a> and why the new version of ribbon doesn&#39;t seem to recognize it?  Is the best strategy for me to learn about the guts of ggplot2 and dig into the code itself?  If so, how should I begin?  I have Hadley&#39;s book from about 2010, but I don&#39;t think it goes this deep into things and it&#39;s maybe outdated too for ggplot2_2.2.0.</div><div><br></div><div>Andy</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"padding:5px;overflow:auto;width:auto;max-height:600px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;color:rgb(57,51,24);word-wrap:normal;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\"><span style=\"color:gray\"># sample data - should be provided in question</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\nset.seed</span><span style=\"color:black\">(</span><span style=\"color:maroon\">1</span><span style=\"color:black\">)</span><span style=\"color:black\">      </span><span style=\"color:gray\"># for reproducible example</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\ntime </span><span style=\"color:black\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:black\"> </span><span style=\"color:maroon\">1</span><span style=\"color:black\">:</span><span style=\"color:maroon\">25</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\ndf   </span><span style=\"color:black\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:black\"> data.frame</span><span style=\"color:black\">(</span><span style=\"color:black\">time</span><span style=\"color:black\">,</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\n                   pop</span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:black\">rnorm</span><span style=\"color:black\">(</span><span style=\"color:maroon\">100</span><span style=\"color:black\">*</span><span style=\"color:black\">length</span><span style=\"color:black\">(</span><span style=\"color:black\">time</span><span style=\"color:black\">),</span><span style=\"color:black\"> mean</span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:maroon\">10</span><span style=\"color:black\">*</span><span style=\"color:black\">time</span><span style=\"color:black\">/(</span><span style=\"color:maroon\">25</span><span style=\"color:black\">+</span><span style=\"color:black\">time</span><span style=\"color:black\">)))</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\n\r\nlibrary</span><span style=\"color:black\">(</span><span style=\"color:black\">ggplot2</span><span style=\"color:black\">)</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\nggplot</span><span style=\"color:black\">(</span><span style=\"color:black\">df</span><span style=\"color:black\">,</span><span style=\"color:black\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:black\">(</span><span style=\"color:black\">x</span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:black\">time</span><span style=\"color:black\">,</span><span style=\"color:black\"> y</span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:black\">pop</span><span style=\"color:black\">))+</span><span style=\"color:black\"> \r\n  stat_summary</span><span style=\"color:black\">(</span><span style=\"color:black\">geom</span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:maroon\">&quot;ribbon&quot;</span><span style=\"color:black\">,</span><span style=\"color:black\"> fun.data</span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:black\">mean_cl_normal</span><span style=\"color:black\">,</span><span style=\"color:black\"> width</span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:maroon\">0.1</span><span style=\"color:black\">,</span><span style=\"color:black\"> <a href=\"http://conf.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://conf.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368230643000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0n_nlcWgE5gWSaLLKp4JXT\">conf.int</a></span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:maroon\">0.95</span><span style=\"color:black\">,</span><span style=\"color:black\"> fill</span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:maroon\">&quot;lightblue&quot;</span><span style=\"color:black\">)+</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\n  stat_summary</span><span style=\"color:black\">(</span><span style=\"color:black\">geom</span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:maroon\">&quot;line&quot;</span><span style=\"color:black\">,</span><span style=\"color:black\"> fun.y</span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:black\">mean</span><span style=\"color:black\">,</span><span style=\"color:black\"> linetype</span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:maroon\">&quot;dashed&quot;</span><span style=\"color:black\">)+</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\n  stat_summary</span><span style=\"color:black\">(</span><span style=\"color:black\">geom</span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:maroon\">&quot;point&quot;</span><span style=\"color:black\">,</span><span style=\"color:black\"> fun.y</span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:black\">mean</span><span style=\"color:black\">,</span><span style=\"color:black\"> color</span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:maroon\">&quot;red&quot;</span><span style=\"color:black\">)</span></code></pre></div></div>"
